<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (We chose BGE-M3 over E5-base because it reads up to 8192 tokens and supports Kazakh better; E5-base stops at 512 tokens. We chose GPT-5.4 Mini over a local Qwen3-4B because it supports structured output and needs no GPU. Qwen3-4B stays as an option for private data.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (We chose a staged pipeline over a single prompt: one stage extracts requirements, one checks them against company documents, one writes the report. Each step can be checked and explained. We keep vectors in PostgreSQL with pgvector instead of a separate vector database, and use plain Python with Pydantic instead of a heavy agent framework. The single prompt stays as a baseline to prove the stages help.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
